 8 of Hearts, 3 of Diamonds, and Jack of Hearts. You currently have "High Card Ten," which has very little showdown value and no significant draws (no straight or flush possibilities). The opponent has shown passivity by checking pre-flop and on the flop, suggesting they likely also have a weak hand or are pot-controlling a marginal hand. However, attempting to bluff here is risky because the board contains high cards (King, Jack) that connect well with many random hands. Since you are currently in the lead in the overall game standings (+700 chips), preserving your stack is prioritized over fighting for a small pot with a garbage hand. The option to check (0) allows you to see the River card for free, potentially hitting a pair or reaching a cheap showdown, without risking any chips.\n\nReason:\nWith no made hand and no draws, betting would be a pure bluff with low probability of success against a board containing a King and a Jack. Since the action is on you and checking is free, checking maximizes the expected value by minimizing loss.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
