ins a flush draw (two diamonds) and straight possibilities. Your opponent has shown extreme passivity by checking pre-flop, on the flop, and on the turn. While you likely have the best hand, your weak kicker makes your hand vulnerable to better Kings if the opponent is slow-playing, and you want to avoid facing a check-raise. Checking back controls the pot size, prevents you from being blown off your equity, and allows you to catch a bluff or value bet safely on the river.\n\nReason: With Top Pair and a weak kicker, checking is the optimal line for pot control. It minimizes the risk of losing a large pot to a better King while keeping the opponent's range wide, potentially inducing bluffs on the river.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
